# Branch Feature: Branch Features

## Score
- 1

## Intent
Define how local Harbormaster extensions are represented inside a host project so they can be reviewed for possible promotion to core Harbormaster.

## Directives
- Branch features are local project-level extensions to Harbormaster behavior.
- Each branch feature must be documented in `.harbormaster/branches/`.
- Each branch feature must be self-contained in a single directives file.
- File naming format: `<feature-name>.branch`.
- Each branch file should include intent, directives, and any compatibility notes.
- Each branch file should include a `Score` value.
- Score definition: number of times the branch has been copied to another Harbormaster project.
- Higher score indicates higher likelihood of promotion into core Harbormaster.
- Branch features should be written so they can be reviewed later in the main Harbormaster project as potential add-ons to core.

## Review notes
- Keep scope explicit and bounded.
- Include migration notes when a branch feature is likely to become core.
